@startuml
title 04 — Workflow Human Input

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Covers two connected moments when a workflow step needs human data:
'
'   PART A — Business Agent signals "I need input at this step"
'     The Orchestrator tries to auto-fill values from prior task
'     outputs so the user doesn't have to do it manually.
'     If auto-fill is not possible, a form is sent to the user.
'
'   PART B — User submits the form
'     The Orchestrator forwards the submitted values to the
'     Workflow API and advances the paused workflow step.
'     The Business Agent (Diagram 05) then continues from where
'     it left off.
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

hide footbox
autonumber "<b>[00]"

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam wrapWidth 260
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor        #2D6A9F
  ArrowFontColor    #2D6A9F
  ArrowFontSize     11

  LifeLineBorderColor         #2D6A9F
  LifeLineBackgroundColor     #EAF3FB

  ParticipantBorderColor      #2D6A9F
  ParticipantBackgroundColor  #DAEAF7
  ParticipantFontColor        #1A3A52
  ParticipantFontSize         12
  ParticipantFontStyle        bold
  ParticipantPadding          8
  ParticipantBorderThickness  1.5

  ActorBorderColor            #1A3A52
  ActorBackgroundColor        #B8D6EE
  ActorFontColor              #1A3A52
  ActorFontSize               12
  ActorFontStyle              bold

  GroupBorderColor            #5A9ABF
  GroupBackgroundColor        #F0F7FC
  GroupHeaderFontColor        #1A3A52
  GroupHeaderFontSize         12
  GroupBorderThickness        1.2

  NoteBackgroundColor         #FFF8DC
  NoteBorderColor             #C8A800
  NoteFontColor               #4A3800
  NoteFontSize                11
}

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8

' ─── Participants ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
participant Orch        as "Orchestrator"
database    DB          as "HANA DB"
participant WorkflowAPI as "Workflow API"
participant Push        as "Push Gateway"
actor       User        as "User / UI"

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
== User Submits the Form ==
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

User -> Orch : POST /orchestrate/agent-action\n(submitted field values + reference to the workflow step)
activate Orch

note over Orch
  The version tag (etag) from Part A is used here to ensure the
  Orchestrator does not overwrite changes made by another process
  between when the form was sent and when the user submitted it.
end note

Orch -> WorkflowAPI : GET current step data + version tag\n(to verify nothing changed while the user was filling the form)
WorkflowAPI --> Orch : current data + version tag

Orch -> WorkflowAPI : PATCH submitted values using the version tag\n(prevents conflicting writes)
WorkflowAPI --> Orch : values saved

Orch -> WorkflowAPI : submit this workflow step\n(signals the workflow to continue)
WorkflowAPI --> Orch : step advanced

Orch -> DB : save a record of this user action\n(so it appears in the conversation history)

Orch --> User : 202 Accepted
deactivate Orch

@enduml
